# Trained model artifacts (*.joblib) are written here by the training scripts.
#
# The files themselves are intentionally NOT committed: they are large binaries
# that bloat git history, and a pickle is tied to the exact library versions
# that produced it. Build them locally or fetch them in CI/deploy.
#
# Expected filenames (see config.py):
#   categorizer.joblib     - text pipeline exposing predict_proba
#   anomaly_scorer.joblib  - estimator exposing score_samples
#
# With no artifacts present the module runs on heuristics, which is a fully
# supported mode - nothing here is required for the API to work.
